Trying not to make any abrupt movements, you carefully take the canister of herbicide with your free hand, remove the stopper with your teeth, and shower the predatory branch adhered to your arm. The fuzz, covered with shining drops, begins to turn dark and shrink before your eyes, but the stubborn plant keeps holding you. Quite a lot of time passes before the substance finally kills the clammy fuzz stuck to your arm. You step back very carefully and fall powerlessly on the grass, gasping for air.

When you recover completely, you go back. Now it is clear that the path through the lilac plants is deadly dangerous, so you have no other option but to make your way through the thick shrubs of white flower bushes.